---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Base
  title="About"
  description="What Leonida Racing is — a GTA VI racing database and community with The Garage, Time Attack and The Hub — what it doesn't do, and who runs it."
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1 class="display page-title">About Leonida Racing</h1>
      <p class="page-lede">Set a lap. Prove it. Find your race.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <div class="wrap prose-body">
      <h2>What this is</h2>
      <p>Leonida Racing is a racing database and community for GTA VI. The database side collects checkable facts — vehicles and their classes, and lap times backed by proof. The community side brings drivers together — race events and the crews behind them. It has three parts:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>The Garage</strong> — the GTA VI vehicles confirmed so far, with their verified in-game classes. Prices, top speeds and lap data are added once they can be checked.</li>
        <li><strong>Time Attack</strong> — a public, proof-based lap-time competition, starting with Gellhorn International Raceway. You submit a lap, and the site answers a few concrete questions for you: what your best comparable run is, where you stand overall and with that specific car, how far you are from the record and from your next realistic target, and — just as important — how solid the time you're looking at actually is and which rule version it was set under.</li>
        <li><strong>The Hub</strong> — an event calendar and crew directory for the racing scene: race nights, league rounds, car meets and the crews behind them. Until the scene forms after release, much of it is clearly marked sample data.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What this isn't (yet)</h2>
      <p>This site doesn't try to be everything. It doesn't rank vehicles independently of the driver — that's a separate, harder question that needs multiple drivers and paired testing, and it only makes sense once enough Time Attack data exists. It's also not a GTA news site, a social feed or a video host.</p>

      <h2>Built ahead of launch</h2>
      <p>GTA VI hasn't come out yet. Everything here — the submission flow, the verification tiers, the rules — is built and ready for release day, but the actual Gellhorn Standard stays in draft until it's been tested against real gameplay. Nothing on this site should be read as a final ruling on how GTA VI works until that testing has happened.</p>

      <h2>Who's behind it</h2>
      <p>Leonida Racing is run by Alexander Jaeger and built with and for the GTA VI racing community. It has no connection to Rockstar Games or Take-Two Interactive — it's an independent community project, not an official one.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions, feedback or moderation requests: reach out on <a href="https://discord.gg/hPGuBwXRqT" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Discord</a>, or by email — see the <a href={`${base}legal/`}>legal notice</a> for the address.</p>

      <h2>How your data is used, briefly</h2>
      <p>Signing in uses Discord. We receive your Discord ID, username, avatar and email address, and Discord asks you to let us add you to our Discord server — that happens once, right after you sign in. Submitting a lap stores the time, vehicle and your evidence screenshot so it can be checked and shown on the leaderboard. Full details, legal bases and retention: <a href={`${base}privacy/`}>Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-band">
    <div class="wrap cta-row">
      <div>
        <h2 class="display cta-title">Get involved</h2>
        <p class="cta-copy">Join the Discord to follow progress, or read the rules to see how submissions work.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cta-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-outline" href={`${base}time-attack/rules/`}>Read the Rules</a>
        <a class="btn btn-red" href="https://discord.gg/hPGuBwXRqT" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Join Discord</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-head { padding-block: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 4.5rem) clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem); }
  .page-title { margin: .6rem 0 .9rem; font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4.5vw, 3.2rem); }
  .page-lede { max-width: 46ch; color: var(--gh-muted); font-size: 1.02rem; }

  .prose { padding-bottom: var(--gh-gap-section); }
  .prose-body { max-width: 62ch; }
  .prose-body h2 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 2.2rem 0 .7rem; }
  .prose-body h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .prose-body p { margin: 0 0 1rem; color: var(--gh-muted); font-size: .96rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .prose-body ul { margin: 0 0 1rem; padding-left: 1.1rem; display: grid; gap: .6rem; color: var(--gh-muted); font-size: .96rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .prose-body li strong { color: var(--gh-text); }

  .cta-band { padding-block: var(--gh-gap-section); border-top: 1px solid var(--gh-line); background: var(--gh-surface-soft); }
  .cta-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 2rem; }
  .cta-title { margin: 0 0 .5rem; font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.6vw, 2rem); }
  .cta-copy { margin: 0; max-width: 42ch; color: var(--gh-muted); font-size: .95rem; }
  .cta-actions { display: flex; gap: .75rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
</style>
